      {
        "id": 54791,
        "name": "Video Olympics",
        "summary": "Video Olympics a collection of games from Atari's popular arcade Pong series is one of the nine 2600 launch titles. The games are a collection of \"bat and ball\" style games, including several previously released by Atari as coin-ops in the early 1970s. The games are played using the 2600s paddle controllers and are for one to four players (three or four players requires a second set of paddle controllers).\n\nEach of the 10 main games have several variations to count the total of 50 games.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co9id7.jpg",
